/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `packages` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `packages` VALUES (1,'Anemia',232,205,25,'Not Required','Anemia is a medical condition where the number of red blood cells in the body is low. The red blood cells are responsible for carrying oxygen to all the organs and tissues in the body, so when they are low on concentration the body does not get enough oxygen to perform well. A complete hemogram or complete blood count test is done to confirm if the individual is suffering from anemia. A complete hemogram test mainly includes Red blood cells, Hemoglobin, Hematocrit, Platelet count, and white blood cells.'),(2,'Allergy',726,642,26,'Not Required','Allergy test is a series of medical tests that is usually performed to determine the kind of allergy that one might be suffering from and what might have caused it. This package contains the IgE antibody test, which helps in identifying the specific allergens that might be causing the specific symptoms that you are expencering. Some of the common symptoms of allergy include diarrhea, wheezing, coughing, sneezing, watery & itchy eyes, and a running nose.'),(3,'Arthritis',1681,1488,61,'12 hours','Arthritis Package helps in screening for any problems related to bones and joints. If you are experiencing any sort of redness, inflammation, swelling, stiffness, pain in joints, etc, you should get screened for Arthritis profile. This is usually for people of old age or family history of arthritis, or someone with obesity, tend to fall in the risk factor for arthritis.'),(4,'Alcoholism',712,629,39,'12 hours','Regular consumption of alcohol comes with various side effects; alcohol has direct impact on the liver health. Routine tests will help in early detection and diagnosis for any kind of liver diseases.'),(5,'Acidity',1088,963,57,'12 hours','Acidity is a very common condition which almost everyone would have experienced in our lives. Even though acidity is quite common, not a lot of people know the actual cause of why it happens. A ring of muscle called the lower esophageal spincter acts as a valve at the entry of stomach. Usually it closes as soon as a person consumes food, however if there is a problem in it closing or if it opens up too often then the acid produced in the stomach moves up to the oesophagus causing a burning sensation known as acidity. If this occurs multiple times a week then it might indicate GERD, and if you suffer from acidity regularly then you might consider an acidity test.'),(6,'Vitamin',799,771,3,'10 hours','Vitamins are essential for our body’s growth and development. Deficiency of vitamins can hamper our bodies’ growth and development. In the vitamins package, you would get the comprehensive vitamins i.e. the Vitamin B12 Cyanocobalamin and Vitamin D Total 25-Hydroxy as well as calcium test. This test can be done on non-fasting mode at any point of the day.'),(7,'Thyroid',260,230,3,'Not Required','A Thyroid function test usually includes a T3, T4 and TSH test where the T4 test is used to determine the amount of thyroxine and a higher level of T4 indicated Hyperthyroidism. The TSH test measures the amount of thyroid stimulating hormone and a higher TSH indicated Hypothyroidism; and the T3 test is used to measure triiodothyronine.'),(8,'Diabetes',365,323,3,'12 hours','Diabetes package is a set of blood tests used for the diagnosis, monitoring and treatment of diabetes. It is recommended for people who have strong risk factors for diabetes and heart diseases like family history of chronic diseases, sedentary lifestyles, alcohol consumption, smoking history and obesity. In addition, this diabetic package can be used to monitor the effectiveness of the continued treatment measures taken for an individual with diabetes.'),(9,'Basic Full Body Check-Up',699,640,87,'12 hours','Unhealthy lifestyles, stress and work life imbalances can gradually take a big toll on our health as we grow older. Early detection and diagnosis is the absolute way forward towards maintaining good health and living disease free. An advanced full body checkup gives a comprehensive view of our health conditions with comprehensive range of tests such as Complete Hemogram, Lipid Profile to check for cholesterol levels, Thyroid Profile to check for thyroid levels, Kidney and Liver profile for good health, Calcium level for bone health, FBS and HbA1c for diabetes level, urine routine for any infections involving urinary tracts. This test needs to be performed with atleast 6-8 hours of fasting from the time of sample collection.'),(10,'Heart',4452,3938,72,'12 hours','Cholesterol is an essential substance for the healthy functioning of the body. However an excessive cholesterol can be a high risk factor for many heart diseases. Cholesterol is a waxy substance that helps your body in building new cells, producing hormones, and insulating nerves. Generally the liver makes cholesterol necessary for the body to perform these functions. However, several food items also have cholesterol in them like - meat, eggs, milk etc. Getting a heart test done is the best way to access if you have any risk factors for heart conditions.'),(11,'Bone',822,727,3,'Not Required','Bones weakness can cause a lot of troubles and nutrition deficiency is the primary reason for it. A calcium level of 10.5 is normal for an individual above 21 years old but signals the presence of a parathyroid tumor in an adult over 40 years old. Teenagers with hyperparathyroidism typically have blood calcium levels between 10.9 and 12.3. Vitamin D is necessary for varied reasons includes bone and tooth health. You may have a vitamin D deficiency if you have bone pain and muscular weakness. The best approach to keep the track of your vitamin D levels is to take the Vitamin D Total-25 Hydroxy test.'),(12,'Fatigue',721,637,5,'Not Required','Fatigue is a condition wherein an individual feels tiredness or have a feeling of lack of energy, wherein the individual may not feel capable of doing any daily activities. Some people might confuse fatigue with a feeling of being sleepy, however they are not the same. Fatigue occurs in a varied of medical conditions such as poor nutrition or certain underlying diseases. A Fatigue test can help you in diagnosing if your fatigue is due to certain underlying medical condition, a deficiency or something else.'),(13,'Male Hormone',384,340,1,'Not Required','Testosterone, the male sex hormone measures the amount of testosterone in a sample of your blood. A total testosterone test measures the free testosterone and testosterone that’s attached to proteins. You may need this test if you have symptoms of abnormal testosterone levels. For males who have gone through puberty, this test is mostly used for symptoms of low Testosterone levels. Testosterone levels tend to usually decrease with the age. A few of the symptoms of low testosterone may include low sex drive, Erectile disfunction, Infertility, enlarged breasts, lack of face or body hair, Thinning bones or anemia without a known cause and loss of muscle mass.'),(14,'Female Hormone',941,831,3,'Not Required','The Female Hormone package comprises of Luteinizing Hormone (LH), Follicle Stimulating Hormone (FSH) and Prolactin. The LH Test measures the level of luteinizing hormone in your blood; LH is made by the pituitary gland, a small gland located underneath the brain. LH plays an important role in sexual development and functioning. In women, LH helps control the menstrual cycle. FSH is made by the pituitary gland plays an integral part as well in the sexual development and functioning. Doctors can check FSH levels using a blood test to access the fertility or see if a person is going through menopause. Doctors advise this test alongside other sex hormones such as testosterone or estrogen.'),(15,'Immunity',499,441,26,'Not Required','The immune system is an essential part of being healthy wherein the immune system works as the body’s defense system that is made up of various types of cells that are constantly working to keep your body safe from bacteria, viruses, parasites, toxins etc. A strong immune system is necessary for leading a healthy and happy life because if you are immunocompromised then you are susceptible to illness. If you suspect that you might have a week immune system then getting an immunity test is the best way to determine and diagnose your condition.'),(16,'Jaundice',374,330,30,'Not Required','Jaundice is a condition wherein the skin, sclera (whites of the eyes) and mucous membranes turn yellow. This yellow colour is caused by a high level of bilirubin, a yellow orange bile pigment. Bile is fluid secreted by the liver and bilirubin is formed from the breakdown of red blood cells.'),(17,'Kidney',254,225,10,'Not Required','Kidney function Test (KFT) are a panel of tests which are required when symptoms of kidney disorders are noticed such as urinary tract infection, diabetes, high blood pressure, kidney stones and excessive use of pain killers. Frequent urination, blood or pain while passing urine, swelling of hands and feet are common symptoms. Timely screening can help in avoiding illness and keep a track of health in best way.'),(18,'Obesity',699,640,87,'12 hours','Obesity is a medical condition wherein an individual body mass index or BMI is equal to or more than 30. Obesity could lead to serious medical condition that has a potential risk of severe illness including diabetes, stroke, cardiac issues, arthritis, fatty liver, thyroid issues and even certain types of cancer. If you are someone with BMI above 30 or you are someone who is overweight, the obesity package would help you determine the organ health better and take timely actions and measures for better health.'),(19,'STD',1117,1077,4,'Not Required','A sexually transmitted infection is spread from one person to another through sexual interaction. A person might contract the disease by having unprotected sex which could be oral, vaginal or anal with someone who has STD. Sex alone is not the method of spread for STDs, infection can also be spread by sharing needles and nursing depending upon the STD. In case of multiple sexual partners, it is advisable to undergo STD tests once in 6 months to prevent, early detect and treat sexual infections.'),(20,'Dengue',921,815,26,'Not Required','Dengue is a mosquito borne viral disease occuring in tropical and subtropical areas. Those who become infected with the virus a second time are at a significantly greater risk of developing severe diseases. The symptoms of dengue includes high fever, headache, rash and muscle and joint pain. In severe cases there is a serious bleeding and shock which can be life threatening.\r\nA dengue NS1 antigen test is used to detect the presence of dengue virus infection, where a positive NS1 test result confirms dengue virus infection without providing serotype information. A negative NS1 test result however does not rule out the infection. People with negative NS1 result should be tested for the presence of dengue IgM antibodies to determine the possible recent dengue exposure.\r\n'),(21,'Malaria',554,490,2,'Not Required','Malaria is a disease caused by parasitic species - plasmodium, the different subsp. Under plasmodium is plasmodium oval, plasmodium vivax and the most lethal one plasmodium falciparum.\r\nPeople who get infected by malaria are typically very sick with high fevers, shaking chillsm, and flu-like illness. In some cases people may experience pain in abdomen or muscles, whole body chills, fatigue, night sweats, shivering or sweating as well as diarrhea, nausea or vomiting.'),(22,'Heartburn',712,629,39,'12 hours','Heartburn is a burning sensation and pain in chest behind the breastbone. The pain is often worse after consuming food in the evening or when lying down or bending over. Occasional heartburn is common and there is no cause for alarm however if the heartburn is more frequent or interfere with daily routine then it may be a symptom of a more serious condition that requires medical care.'),(23,'Junk Food',1220,1079,58,'12 hours','Regular consumption of junk food posses a risk of long term effect on health and wellbeing on an individual. With increase in the consumption of fast food, one may experience Gastrointestinal issues like GERD, increased in cholesterol level. Increased cholesterol level has a direct impact on the cardiac health of an individual. Regular consumption of junk food also posses a risk of an individual becoming overweight and obese. Junk food blood test package helps you understand your health better with LFT levels helping in detecting the presence of gall stones and renal function test and Urine routine helps in understing the presence of renal stones and acute urinary tract infections, blood glucose fasting test helps in determining the potential risk of an individual getting diabetes or being in prediabetic\r\ncondition. Depending upon the lifestyle choices, an individual with increased consumption of junk food is advised to get a Junk food package test done once in every 3-4 months.'),(24,'Anger',469,415,13,'12 hours',NULL),(25,'Low Iron Diet',215,190,4,'Not Required',NULL),(26,'Poor Nutrition',1895,1675,33,'10 hours','Poor nutrition can result in lack of various macro and micro nutrients in the body. Lack of vitamins also known as Hypovitaminosis can result in various health disorders, such as deficiency of vitamin D can result in incorrect growth patterns due to bowed or bent bones, muscle weakness, bone pain and deformities in joints. In certain case deficiency of vitamin D can show signs of depression as well. Vitamin B12 deficiency may lead to a reduction of healthy red blood cells causing anemia. Symptoms of low vitamin B12 are rare but can include fatigue, numbness, breathlessness, poor balance and memory trouble.'),(27,'Smoking',712,629,39,'12 hours',NULL),(28,'Zero Exercise',1248,1104,36,'12 hours',NULL),(29,'Stress',358,316,1,'Not Required','Stress is a feeling of either emotional or physical tension which can come from any event or thought that makes you feel frustrated, angry or nervous. In short bursts, stress can be positive, such as when it helps you avoid danger or meet certain deadlines, however when a stress lasts for a long time, it may harm your health. Stress can cause many types of emotional and physical symptoms. Here are some of the signs that stress may be affecting you could be forgetfulness, stiff jaw or stiff neck, headaches, sexual problems, tiredness, either trouble with sleeping or sleeping too much, diarrhea or constipation, weight loss or weight gain, upset stomach, increased use of alcohol, cigarettes or drugs to relax. \r\nA serum cortisol test is used to measure the level of cortisol in your body. Cortisol, also known as the stress hormone is important to several bodily functions. Cortisol testing requires a sample of blood, urine, saliva or a combination of all.'),(30,'Sleeplessness',1606,420,37,'12 hours',NULL),(31,'Medicine Overdose',610,539,53,'Not Required',NULL),(32,'Advance Full Body Check-Up',1199,1199,89,'12 hours','Unhealthy lifestyles, stress and work life imbalances can gradually take a big toll on our health as we grow older. Early detection and diagnosis is the absolute way forward towards maintaining good health and living disease free. An advanced full body checkup gives a comprehensive view of our health conditions with comprehensive range of tests such as Complete Hemogram, Lipid Profile to check for cholesterol levels, Thyroid Profile to check for thyroid levels, Vitamin B12 and D25 Hydroxy to check for Hypovitaminosis, Kidney and Liver profile for good health, Calcium level for bone health, FBS and HbA1c for diabetes level, urine routine for any infections involving urinary tracts. This test needs to be performed with at least 6-8 hours of fasting from the time of sample collection.'),(33,'Gensxty Basic Full Body Check-Up',600,600,87,'8 hours','Unhealthy lifestyles, stress and work life imbalances can gradually take a big toll on our health as we grow older. Early detection and diagnosis is the absolute way forward towards maintaining good health and living disease free. An advanced full body checkup gives a comprehensive view of our health conditions with comprehensive range of tests such as Complete Hemogram, Lipid Profile to check for cholesterol levels, Thyroid Profile to check for thyroid levels, Kidney and Liver profile for good health, Calcium level for bone health, FBS and HbA1c for diabetes level, urine routine for any infections involving urinary tracts. This test needs to be performed with atleast 6-8 hours of fasting from the time of sample collection'),(34,'Gensxty Annual Health Check-Up',1200,1200,100,'12 hours','Unhealthy lifestyles, stress and work life imbalances can gradually take a big toll on our health as we grow older. Early detection and diagnosis is the absolute way forward towards maintaining good health and living disease free. An advanced full body checkup gives a comprehensive view of our health conditions with comprehensive range of tests such as Complete Hemogram, Lipid Profile to check for cholesterol levels, Thyroid Profile to check for thyroid levels, Vitamin B12 and D25 Hydroxy to check for Hypovitaminosis, Kidney and Liver profile for good health, Calcium level for bone health, FBS and HbA1c for diabetes level, urine routine for any infections involving urinary tracts. This test needs to be performed with at least 6-8 hours of fasting from the time of sample collection.'),(35,'Gensxty Sr Citizen Package-Cancer Markers',2200,2200,100,'12 hours','Unhealthy lifestyles, stress and work life imbalances can gradually take a big toll on our health as we grow older the chances of cancer also increases. Cancer is the uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells that can spread to other parts of the body. Common tests include blood tests, imaging (X-rays, CT scans, MRI), biopsies, genetic testing, and endoscopy. Early detection through screenings like mammograms, Pap smears, and tumor markers improves treatment outcomes and increases survival chances.'),(36,'Gensxty Sr Citizen Package-Cardiac Markers',2200,2200,100,'12 hours','Cholesterol is an essential substance for the healthy functioning of the body. However an excessive cholesterol can be a high risk factor for many heart diseases. Cholesterol is a waxy substance that helps your body in building new cells, producing hormones, and insulating nerves. Generally the liver makes cholesterol necessary for the body to perform these functions. However, several food items also have cholesterol in them like - meat, eggs, milk etc. Getting a heart test done is the best way to access if you have any risk factors for heart conditions. ');
